{"kind":"request","text":"S4 source facts for 63636688, with one capacity ruling.\n\nRegistry connections keeps listing an existing OAuth Agent mapping without a retired flag; non-OAuth Agents without that mapping do not appear. Agent connections reports state retired. Its issuer metadata list is empty after revokeAll commits, but may still show unexpired metadata if a late stop happens before revokeAll. Seed, bearer and Access credentials are already disabled by local retirement. Current authority still guards either private list.\n\nHosted SQL has no numeric per-controller Agent count. A confirmed controller/client mapping can use the existing fresh-creation replacement path after actual retired identity and fresh authority/owner checks. Legacy NULL or provisional mappings cannot use that path. Control tombstones and historical rows continue consuming their object-wide byte budgets.\n\nNative own-Agent admission has a separate limit: eight ACTIVE kind-agent members controlled by the signer. Hosted retirement and revoke-key leave the Native member active, so it occupies that place indefinitely until existing remove-member records removal. An ordinary controller with only membership.own-agent cannot free it alone; membership.manage or recovery authority must perform remove-member. This cap governs the ordinary own-Agent path, not administrative add-member.\n\nMay S4 retain this existing capacity behavior and document that key revocation does not free the member place, naming membership.manage/recovery remove-member as the separate existing action? No automatic removal or new permission is proposed. This question does not block the already ruled response work.\n\nI read the full source trace and checked the actual Native capacity predicate, remove-member/revoke-key effects, Registry queries and staged Issuer revokeAll/list. Trace: /private/tmp/artroom-r3b-design-s4-retirement-connections-capacity-facts-20261111.md, SHA-256 553fa38cd07e2b7529ce5e3eb9ff7afeb33f2f8cef50c5acf066272d901721e8. No application body ran.","body":{"conditions":"Rule only on retaining/documenting the existing Native eight-active-Agent member capacity after Hosted retirement. No new cleanup action, permission, counter reset, operation ownership or deployment.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}